I reviewed the site’s central architecture rather than treating its hundreds of philosopher profiles as independent doctrines. Doyle’s system has six connected pillars:

[
\text{cosmic information creation}
\rightarrow
\text{life}
\rightarrow
\text{memory}
\rightarrow
\text{agency}
\rightarrow
\text{knowledge}
\rightarrow
\text{value}
]

His strongest contribution is the repeated **two-stage architecture**:

[
\boxed{\text{generate alternatives}\rightarrow\text{select and preserve}}
]

His weakest moves are identifying information too quickly with negative entropy, treating abstract information as a causally active quasi-substance, deriving moral value from organized complexity, and assuming quantum randomness is specifically required for agency. Doyle explicitly presents information philosophy as a unified account of free will, value and knowledge grounded in information creation, “soft” causality and an open future. ([Information Philosopher][1])

The scientifically defensible reconstruction is below.

# Constraint-Selection Information Dynamics

## A scientific reconstruction of Information Philosophy

---

## Abstract

Information Philosopher correctly identifies a deep recurrent architecture across physics, biology, cognition and culture:

[
\text{variation}
\rightarrow
\text{selection}
\rightarrow
\text{stabilization}
\rightarrow
\text{reuse}
]

However, its original formulation conflates several distinct quantities:

* thermodynamic entropy;
* Shannon information;
* algorithmic description length;
* causal constraint;
* biological function;
* semantic knowledge;
* moral value.

The present theory separates them.

**Constraint-Selection Information Dynamics**, or **CSID**, proposes that the major transitions from physical structure to life, agency, mind and culture occur when systems acquire increasingly powerful mechanisms for:

1. generating counterfactual alternatives;
2. differentially stabilizing alternatives relative to constraints;
3. preserving selected outcomes in physical memory;
4. using preserved information to regulate future variation;
5. modelling their own uncertainty and possible actions.

The fundamental object is not “information” considered as an immaterial substance. It is a materially realized difference that constrains future state transitions.

Formally:

[
\boxed{
\text{effective information}
============================

\text{physically preserved constraint on possible futures}
}
]

Doyle’s two-stage model is retained but generalized:

[
\boxed{
\text{exploration}
\rightarrow
\text{constraint-sensitive selection}
}
]

This architecture appears in evolutionary variation and selection, learning, immune adaptation, morphogenesis, deliberation, creativity and cultural inquiry. It does not by itself prove libertarian free will, consciousness or objective moral value. It supplies a testable theory of how novelty becomes agency and knowledge.

