# II. The five information concepts that must be separated

## 1. Thermodynamic entropy

For a macrostate with compatible microstates (W):

[
S_{\mathrm{th}}
===============

k_B\ln W
]

Thermodynamic entropy concerns physical multiplicity and energy dispersal.

A local system may decrease its entropy while increasing the entropy of its environment:

[
\Delta S_{\mathrm{system}}<0
]

while:

[
\Delta S_{\mathrm{system}}
+
\Delta S_{\mathrm{environment}}
\geq0
]

Living organisms are thermodynamically open and maintain organization through sustained matter and energy exchange. ([PubMed Central (PMC)][5])

## 2. Shannon information

For random variable (X):

[
H(X)
====

-\sum_xp(x)\log p(x)
]

This measures uncertainty relative to a specified distribution.

High Shannon entropy may mean:

* high uncertainty;
* high signal variety;
* high randomness.

It does not automatically mean:

* disorder in an ordinary visual sense;
* biological organization;
* meaning;
* intelligence;
* value.

## 3. Algorithmic information

For object (x), Kolmogorov complexity is approximately:

[
K(x)
====

\min_{p:U(p)=x}|p|
]

It measures the length of the shortest program producing (x).

A random sequence normally has high (K(x)), but high algorithmic complexity does not imply meaningful organization.

## 4. Causal information

A variable carries causal information when intervention on it changes another variable:

[
I_{\mathrm{causal}}(X\rightarrow Y)

> 0
> ]

iff:

[
P(Y\mid do(X=x))
]

varies with (x).

This is closer to what matters for organisms: differences that alter possible trajectories.

## 5. Semantic or functional information

A signal (s) has functional information for system (A) when its interpretation affects the system’s capacity to maintain or achieve relevant states:

[
I_{\mathrm{functional}}(s;A)>0
]

iff removing, randomizing or replacing (s) predictably reduces some system-relative capacity:

[
P(G_A\mid s)

>

P(G_A\mid \operatorname{scramble}(s))
]

Biological uses of “information” therefore need more than Shannon correlation; they often involve evolved signalling, causal roles, representations or system-relative function. ([Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy][6])

## Separation theorem

In general:

[
S_{\mathrm{th}}
\neq
H
\neq
K
\neq
I_{\mathrm{causal}}
\neq
I_{\mathrm{functional}}
]

Relations may exist in particular models, but none are universally interchangeable.

Therefore Doyle’s recurring equation:

[
\text{information}
\approx
\text{negative entropy}
]

must be replaced by:

[
\boxed{
\text{Some low-entropy physical structures embody information,
but organization, uncertainty, causation and meaning require distinct measures.}
}
]

