# IV. Information creation

Doyle’s phrase “creation of information” contains three different processes.

## 1. Generation of variation

A system produces a distribution over possible states:

[
q(z\mid x)
]

Sources may include:

* thermal fluctuations;
* quantum events;
* chaotic sensitivity;
* mutation;
* recombination;
* stochastic gene expression;
* exploratory behaviour;
* internally generated simulations.

This generates alternatives but not necessarily useful organization.

## 2. Differential stabilization

A selection operator (S_C) acts relative to constraints (C):

[
S_C:q(z\mid x)\rightarrow q'(z\mid x,C)
]

where selected states have unequal persistence or reproduction probabilities:

[
P(\operatorname{persist}(z_i)\mid C)
\neq
P(\operatorname{persist}(z_j)\mid C)
]

## 3. Memory

A selected outcome modifies a persistent variable (m_t):

[
m_{t+1}
=======

M(m_t,z_t,C_t)
]

Memory exists when the past remains causally available:

[
I(m_t;z_{t-\tau})>0
]

and changes future transitions:

[
P(x_{t+1}\mid x_t,m_t)
\neq
P(x_{t+1}\mid x_t)
]

## Creation theorem

Novel functional information arises when:

[
\boxed{
\text{variation}
+
\text{differential stabilization}
+
\text{memory}
}
]

jointly increase future constraint-sensitive capacity.

Define adaptive information gain:

[
\Delta I_A
==========

## I(G_A;X_{t+1}\mid M_{t+1})

I(G_A;X_{t+1}\mid M_t)
]

where (G_A) denotes a relevant target or viability condition.

Then:

[
\Delta I_A>0
]

means the system’s updated memory better constrains action or development toward (G_A).

Randomness alone does not create adaptive information:

[
\operatorname{RandomVariation}
\not\Rightarrow
\Delta I_A>0
]

Selection alone cannot create alternatives absent variation:

[
\operatorname{Selection}
\land
|\mathcal Z|=1
\not\Rightarrow
\text{novelty}
]

Memory is required for cumulative improvement:

[
\operatorname{Variation}
+
\operatorname{Selection}
------------------------

\operatorname{Memory}
\Rightarrow
\text{repeated search without accumulation}
]

Therefore:

[
\boxed{
\text{Cumulative novelty requires generation, selection and retention.}
}
]

