# XXIII. Final scientific theory statement

[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
\textbf{Constraint-Selection Information Dynamics holds that:}[4pt]
\text{The physically important form of information is persistent organization}\
\text{that changes the probability distribution over a system's possible futures.}[4pt]
\text{Novel adaptive information arises when variation is differentially selected}\
\text{relative to constraints, preserved in memory, and reused to regulate later variation.}[4pt]
\text{Life begins when historically selected constraints recursively maintain}\
\text{the organization that embodies them.}[4pt]
\text{Agency increases when a system generates counterfactual alternatives,}\
\text{evaluates them relative to endogenous goals, enacts selected policies,}\
\text{and learns from their consequences.}[4pt]
\text{Knowledge arises when preserved models support prediction and intervention}\
\text{and remain corrigible under counterevidence.}[4pt]
\text{Operational freedom is the capacity for reason-sensitive, historically informed}\
\text{and self-modifying control over multiple possible futures.}
\end{aligned}
}
]

The compact form is:

[
Z_t\sim G(M_t,E_t)
]

[
z_t^*\sim S(Z_t\mid C_t,M_t)
]

[
X_{t+1}=\Phi(X_t,z_t^*,E_t)
]

[
M_{t+1}=U(M_t,X_t,z_t^*,X_{t+1})
]

[
\boxed{
\mathbb E[\Delta I(M;G_{\mathrm{future}})]>0
}
]

This is Doyle’s surviving scientific core:

[
\boxed{
\text{possibility}
\rightarrow
\text{selection}
\rightarrow
\text{memory}
\rightarrow
\text{control}
\rightarrow
\text{knowledge}
}
]

The theory rejects three unnecessary additions:

[
\text{information}\neq\text{immaterial causal substance}
]

[
\text{randomness}\neq\text{freedom}
]

[
\text{organization}\neq\text{moral goodness}
]

Its strongest final conclusion is:

[
\boxed{
\text{The arrow from matter to mind is not an increase in information quantity.
It is the progressive closure of a loop in which selected information controls
the future generation and selection of information.}
}
]

A rock embodies structure.

A living system uses inherited structure to preserve itself.

An agent uses acquired structure to select among possible futures.

A mind generates models of futures that do not yet exist.

A reflective mind can alter the machinery by which those futures are generated and judged.

That—rather than quantum randomness or negative entropy alone—is the scientifically tractable core of informational freedom.

The crucial upgrade over Doyle is:

[
\boxed{
\text{information creation}
\longrightarrow
\text{adaptive constraint accumulation}
}
]

This makes the theory measurable. It also integrates cleanly with Levin: morphogenetic intelligence becomes one instance of the same loop—generate possible trajectories, select toward anatomical targets, preserve successful constraints, and reuse them during future repair.

